  "body": "## Summary\n\nConditional \u03ba = **0.001661634653669567**. This is +4.32\u00d710\u207b\u2077 over PR741 (0.001661202643272239). The complex side binds; PR589's bit supplier gives 0.0017334.\n\n**Construction**, on PR699's word (sha d232183f):\n1. **chafreaky's PR741 frames:** the 8 B-gate frame raises (dim 4\u21926), imported byte-identically from PR741's recipe, with its 10 frame mutation controls. This step rebuilds PR741's word e7804702.\n2. **X4, new here: four paired read exchanges.** For each of the copy-pair pairs (448,472), (458,592), (470,604) and (482,614), both pairs' phase-B target reads are exchanged under the PR699 sw4 rule (pre-reads deleted or inserted so every register's end-of-B value is unchanged; exact Fraction check). The moved reads keep their original stored dim-6 frames instead of being refit to the minimal join, and that is where the gain comes from. Each pair on its own is exactly neutral; the two pairs of an instance together give +1.08\u00d710\u207b\u2077, and the four instances are exactly additive. Profile \u0394 {1:\u22128, 2:+4}, widths unchanged (3778).\n\n**Owner map:** PR741's map (the same file as PR699's), unchanged. An exact packing relaxation already proved it optimal for this window geometry, and X4 changes no widths or windows.\n\n**Construction drivers:** `construction/frames/` (PR741's recipe, build and 10 frame controls) and `construction/jx/` (standard-library builder, explicit edit recipe, 7 pinned controls: identity, PR741-only, a single pair is neutral, dropped pre-read and wrong sign rejected by exactness, minimal-join refit is lower, and a dim-7 frame is rejected by the cap). All verifier code is byte-identical to PR699's reviewed set.\n\n**Search coverage:** all 602 single-pair read subsets and all 5,880 combinations over the 40 target-sharing pair-pairs (24 legal, exactly these 4 positive); triples and larger sets were also searched. Three independent searches found the same four instances. An exact global frame optimiser confirms the word is frame-optimal at fixed gate order.\n\n**Independent review:** SOUND (details in the review comment). The reviewer reproduced both steps byte-identically, found the 64 edits equal the sw4 rule, confirmed that no surviving gate changes frame, ran an exact replay (0 bad rows, dyadic, all orientations) and audit_local, checked that all 7 controls hit their pins, and rejected 8 extra mutants.\n\n## Verification\n\nFrom a fresh clone of commit 80e64631, with no reused artifacts (Windows, CPython 3.11.11):\n- `verify_manifest.py`: PASS, 132 files\n- `reproduce.py`, `reproduce_notri.py`, `reproduce_np.py`, `reproduce_p6n.py`, `reproduce_promo.py --k p6n-k4`, `reproduce_sw4.py`: PR699's word rebuilt, with every layer's controls\n- `reproduce_jx.py`: X4 word 1e1d99ba rebuilt, all 7 controls at their pinned outcomes\n- `audit_local.py`: PASS_INDEPENDENT_EXACT_FORWARD_AND_DUAL_ENDPOINT_FRAMES_ENTRANCES_CONES\n- `verify_global.py`: **PASS_GAUGE44_NATIVE_EXACT_GLOBAL_ASSEMBLY 0.001661634653669567**\n\n`construction/frames/reproduce_frames.py` independently rebuilds PR741's word e7804702 (exercised by the reviewer).\n\n## Scope\n\nConditional on PR645's premises and PR589's bit-supplier assumptions. No unconditional theorem or Lean certification is claimed.\n\n## Credits\n\n- **chafreaky** (PR741, PR685, PR660): the 8 frame raises, the owner map and the exact-flow packing.\n- **icekylinx** (PR645): gauge44 construction, package and verifier.\n- PR589 lineage (bit supplier); the PR601/604/617/622/627/635 lineage and every upstream contributor credited in PR645.\n\nPrepared with Claude Code (Anthropic).\n",
